# corpus/scopes.def — canonical scope definition for the C23 corpus census
# (build/bin/corpus-census, tools/corpus_census.c). One scope per line:
#
#   scope <name> | kind <human|ai|import> | spdx <SPDX-ID> \
#       | src <prefix>[,<prefix>...] | tests <prefix>[,<prefix>...]
#
# Prefixes are repo-relative. A trailing '/' means "this directory tree";
# otherwise the prefix is a literal file prefix (e.g. lib/test/src/test_base
# claims lib/test/src/test_base_foundation.c). Only tracked files
# (git ls-files) with a .c/.h/.def extension enter the census.
#
# File-claim precedence (deterministic; ambiguity fails closed): a tests
# claim beats a src claim of another scope; among same-kind claims the
# LONGEST matching prefix wins (so lib/test/src/test_base beats the shared
# lib/test/ remainder); two equal-length competing claims are a fatal
# overlap error. No file is ever counted twice.
#
# kind is DECLARED provenance: no per-file authorship marker exists in-tree,
# so every scope below is declared `human` (pre-existing node code). The
# census report carries this disclosure verbatim.
#
# spdx is bound to a real license file by the driver: a scope-local LICENSE
# when one exists (lib/base, lib/codec, lib/commons_demo, lib/crypto,
# lib/encoding, lib/json, lib/platform, lib/presentation, lib/sha3, lib/vcs),
# otherwise the repo-root LICENSE (Apache-2.0). lib/commons_demo,
# lib/encoding and lib/sha3 carry MIT texts; everything else is Apache-2.0.
#
# vendor/ and core/ are deliberately NOT scopes: vendor/ is third-party
# material (the census would exclude it as VENDOR) and core/ is the
# byte-sealed consensus core, which is not C23 Commons package content.
#
# ── package lines, and why `store` is a LABEL ───────────────────────
#
#   package <name> | root <64hex> | store <label> \
#       | kind <human|ai|import> | spdx <SPDX-ID>
#
# A package scope is enumerated from a published C23 Commons package store
# instead of from git. `store` names WHICH local store to read; it is one
# path component drawn from [A-Za-z0-9._-] (never '.', '..', '/' or '~'),
# and the census resolves it to <store-root>/<label>/zcode, where store-root
# comes from --store-root, else $ZCL_CORPUS_STORE_ROOT, else $HOME.
#
# It is a label and not a path because this line is copied VERBATIM into
# every evidence record (`scopes_def_line`) and hashed into
# assignment_evidence_root. While the field held an absolute datadir, the
# operator's home directory shipped 2,302 times in the committed corpus
# artifacts — a local filesystem locator in a repository whose privacy rule
# is that committed files carry no clearnet address, hostname, username, or
# local path. The path was never what the evidence was ABOUT: `root` is the
# package manifest root, re-derived from the store and refused on mismatch,
# and that is what binds the bytes. Where those bytes sit on one host is an
# operator-local coordinate and belongs in a flag, not in this file.
#
# FLAG DAY: these lines carried `store /home/<user>/<label>` through
# sequence 42. Sequences from 43 on hash the label form, so the sequence-42
# assignment_evidence_root values are NOT reproducible from this file. That
# is recorded rather than hidden — see corpus/README.md.

# ── repo subtrees ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
scope zclassic23/adapters | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src adapters/
scope zclassic23/app | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src app/
scope zclassic23/application | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src application/
scope zclassic23/apps/blog | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src apps/blog/
scope zclassic23/apps/social | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src apps/social/
scope zclassic23/apps/yardsale | kind human | spdx Apache-2.0 | src apps/yardsale/
